From c93ed45fae21e9a2de4d7af4b0ac7ab2ad98e9d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: gts28ltexx: the energy model, for EAS

Each CPU node gets the dynamic-power-coefficient measured on the
tablet: 177 for the A53s, 648 for the A57s (uW/MHz/V^2).  With
CONFIG_ENERGY_MODEL, cpufreq-dt registers one perf domain per cluster
and the scheduler turns energy-aware scheduling on (the capacities were
already in the board file: capacity-dmips-mhz 2048 and 3575).

Measured on the SM-T715, 2026-11-27, screen dark, on the Mac's USB (the
charger at its 450 mA input limit: a change in the system's draw shows
one for one in the battery current), both clusters pinned, three busy
A53 or four busy A57 against idle: per busy core 146 and 280 mW for an
A53 at 800 MHz and 1.2 GHz (C 182, 172), 497 and 896 mW for an A57
(C 636, 661).  The work per clock of an A53 against an A57, at the same
frequency, came out at 0.52-0.74 (Python, xz, gzip); the board's
capacities say 0.573.

With EAS, under a UI-like load (three tasks, a frame of fixed work every
16.7 ms), the work stays on the A53s at about 440 MHz and the A57s idle;
the system draws 76 mW less than with sched_energy_aware=0 (three pairs
of 2-min phases: 7, 138, 82 mW), with 3 late frames in 69518 against 0
in 69788.  A single heavy task still runs on an A57 (2.05-2.3 s against
2.07 s), eight at once take the same time (3.27 s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-eas.dtsi | 37 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts |  1 +
 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-eas.dtsi

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-eas.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-eas.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..53e239b76
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-eas.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Samsung Galaxy Tab S2 8.0 LTE (SM-T715): the energy model of the two
+ * clusters, for energy-aware scheduling (CONFIG_ENERGY_MODEL).
+ *
+ * cpufreq-dt registers each cluster's model from its OPP table and the
+ * dynamic-power-coefficient of its CPU nodes: P[uW] = C * f[MHz] * V[V]^2.
+ * The capacities are the board's (capacity-dmips-mhz 2048 and 3575, in the
+ * 32-bit board file); with both, the scheduler places a task on the cluster
+ * that runs it for the least energy, and a task too big for an A53 on an A57.
+ *
+ * C measured on the reference tablet on 2026-11-27, screen dark, on the
+ * Mac's USB (the charger at its 450 mA input limit, so a change in the
+ * system's draw shows one for one in the battery current): both clusters
+ * pinned to one frequency, three busy A53 or four busy A57 against idle, C2
+ * on.  Power per busy core over idle, and the C it implies at the OPP's
+ * voltage:
+ *
+ *   A53  800 MHz, 1.0000 V:  146 mW  ->  182
+ *   A53 1200 MHz, 1.1625 V:  280 mW  ->  172
+ *   A57  800 MHz, 0.9875 V:  497 mW  ->  636
+ *   A57 1200 MHz, 1.0625 V:  896 mW  ->  661  (the A57s at 64-70 C)
+ *
+ * The model holds across the frequencies within 6 %; each value is the mean
+ * of its two.  An A53 does the same work for less energy than an A57 at
+ * every frequency here (0.48 mW per unit of capacity at 1.2 GHz, against
+ * 0.73 for an A57 at 800 MHz and 0.88 at 1.2 GHz).
+ */
+
+&cpu0 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <177>; };
+&cpu1 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <177>; };
+&cpu2 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <177>; };
+&cpu3 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <177>; };
+&cpu4 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <648>; };
+&cpu5 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <648>; };
+&cpu6 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <648>; };
+&cpu7 { dynamic-power-coefficient = <648>; };
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
index 0717a8ca6..5fca3ffb2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
@@ -12,3 +12,4 @@
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-smp.dtsi"
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-stage1.dtsi"
 #include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-no-sysmmu.dtsi"
+#include "exynos5433-gts28ltexx-eas.dtsi"
